{
  "original": "无可奈何花落去，似曾相识燕归来。",
  "reference_notes": {
    "无可奈何花落去": "无力挽留地看着花落。要点：无奈、无力的情感。",
    "似曾相识燕归来": "归来的燕子仿佛曾经见过。要点：'似曾相识'的模糊感。",
    "花落去vs燕归来": "离去与归来的对比。要点：去与来的对比结构。",
    "时间流逝的感慨": "对时光流逝、物是人非的感慨。要点：时间、变化的主题。"
  },
  "translation": "**English Translation:**",
  "notes": [
    "- The poem uses personification to give human-like qualities to the flower (falling) and the swallow (returning), making these natural phenomena more relatable and emotional.",
    "- \"无可奈何\" (wú kě nài hé) expresses a sense of helplessness or resignation, which is conveyed through the metaphorical references to the flower and the swallow."
  ]
}
